What:		/sys/devices/platform/lis3lv02d/motion
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	6.14
Contact:	Kailash <kailash.sudhakar@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RW) Motion wake of 8-bit lis3lv02d parts that have an
		interrupt. Writing a boolean value (kstrtobool) "1" arms the
		chip's free-fall/wake-up units around the current position;
		the first motion event disarms them and wakes poll() on the
		"position" attribute. Writing "1" again re-arms. Writing "0"
		stops motion watching. Reading returns "1" while armed, "0"
		otherwise. Writing returns -EOPNOTSUPP on parts that are not
		8-bit or have no interrupt.
